# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# Where the build verifies, an operation that stands for one of the input takes, at each operand, what lies within the row of the input operand's maker
# (Walker::takesWhatRowOfInputOperandCannotGive(), walk/AOTWalk.cpp): an Add over a ToString never becomes an Add over a number. Two things are legal and must not ring:
# a Strcat makes a text of every operand itself, so the ToString in front of it may be left out and the number kept; an operator in a form of numbers takes the truth of a comparison as 0 or 1.
